    ["video_files",
    ".VEG",
    "VEGAS Video Project",
    "4.0",
    "A VEG file is a video project created by MAGIX VEGAS Pro, a professional video-editing and disc-authoring application. It contains a record of a projects timeline, including the projects included audio and video tracks, edits, transitions, text content, and special effects. VEG file open in MAGIX VEGAS Pro 16 VEGAS Pro uses VEG files to store video projects, video templates, and archives. In all cases, the VEG file format remains the same. Using a VEG file as a template allows users to maintain the same settings across different projects. By using a VEG file as an archive, you can save backups of projects that you can open at a later time. Select File → Export → VEGAS Project Archive to save your project as an archive. Completed VEGAS Pro projects can be shared online directly from VEGAS Pro. They can also be exported to a variety of digital video formats, including.AAF (Pro Tools or Media Composer),.PRPROJ (Premiere or After Effects), and.FCPXML (Final Cut Pro X). NOTE: VEGAS software was previously developed by Sony before being acquired by MAGIX in 2016. You can open VEG files in MAGIX VEGAS Pro (Windows). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your VEG file. Windows MAGIX VEGAS Pro 18. 3D scene file used by E-on Vue, an environment and atmospheres modeling application; stores plant models that can be incorporated into a Vue scene; can be used for generating fractals of plants on terrains or other landscapes. Windows E-on Vue. Mac E-on Vue.",
    "Windows MAGIX VEGAS Pro 18. Windows E-on Vue. Mac E-on Vue.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".INP",
    "Sony Camcorder Image Management File",
    "4.0",
    "An INP file is a text document created by Urdu InPage, a multilingual publishing application for the Urdu, Arabic, Persian, and English languages. It contains text saved in the Noorinastaliq font, which displays Urdu in nastaliq script. The INP format also supports standard page formatting. Urdu InPage is a Windows program that allows users to create text documents in many different languages. Primarily, users use InPage to create documents written in Urdu. NOTE: While a Mac version of InPage exists, it can be run only using the CrossOver Mac application, which allows Mac users to run Windows applications on their Mac. You can open an INP file in Concept Software Urdu InPage (Windows). There are no other known programs that can open INP files. You can use Urdu InPage to convert INP files to the.PDF format. To do so, open your INP file in InPage, then select File → Save as PDF. Windows Concept Software Urdu InPage. An INP file is an input file used by the Dassault Systemes Abaqus engineering simulation and analysis software suite. It contains plain text input data for a job that produces output visualizations (eg. Abaqus.ODB output databases) and other data. Users may create INP files with the Abaqus/CAE app included in the Abaqus suite or with a text editor. INP file open in Microsoft Visual Studio Code 1.76 Dr. David Hibbitt, Dr. Bengt Karlsson, and Dr. Paul Sorensen initially developed Abaqus (formerly ABAQUS) and released it in 1978. However, Dassault Systemes now develops the software, which is prevalent in various commercial and academic mechanical engineering industries, including aerospace and automotive. INP files store information in two parts: Model data - Defines the mesh structure to be analyzed in Abaqus, which includes structure metadata, nodal coordinates, model definition, and materials. History data - Defines what happens to the structure (each step of loading or events) to create the data for analysis or visualization. You can open an INP file with the Abaqus suite of applications in Windows or Linux. To open an INP file, select File → Import → Model. Since the INP file stores plain text, you can also open them with any text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad (Windows) or Apple TextEdit (macOS). Additionally, Microsoft Visual Studio Code (multiplatform) provides helpful data-viewing and -editing capabilities. Windows Dassault Systemes Abaqus. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor Linux Dassault Systemes Abaqus. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor. Management file created for some Sony digital camcorders; holds metadata about recorded videos and images; located in the AVF_INFO folder along with.BNP and.INT files; should not be modified. If this file is deleted, you will not be able to record or play back video or images correctly. INP files are defaulted as hidden files and usually not displayed. Windows Sony Picture Motion Browser —  (Discontinued). Game replay file created by a MAME arcade emulator; stores the replay using a proprietary MAME compressed format, which allows the file to be smaller in size than a video recorded equivalent; used for playing back recorded games and sharing them online. Windows MAME. ExtraMAME. Mac MacMAME MAME OS XFree. Script file created and used by gretl, an open source econometrics program; contains a command that tells gretl to perform an action, such as tests or calculations on economic data. You can open the INP script file in gretl by selecting File → Script files. NOTE: The INP file is created and overwritten whenever you start a new session. Windows gretl. Mac gretlFree.",
    "Windows Concept Software Urdu InPage. Windows Dassault Systemes Abaqus. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor. Linux Dassault Systemes Abaqus. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor. Windows Sony Picture Motion Browser —  (Discontinued). Windows MAME. ExtraMAME. Mac MacMAME MAME OS X. Windows gretl. Mac gretl.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".PLOTDOC",
    "Plotagon Project File",
    "4.0",
    "A PLOTDOC file is a text file created by previous versions of Plotagon Studio. It is a JSON file that describes a Plotagon project. PLOTDOC files have been replaced by.PLOT files. Animation enthusiasts use Plotagon Studio to create, edit, and publish 3D animated movies. Plotagon Studio movies typically include animated scenes, subtitles, and spoken dialogue. In the past, Plotagon created PLOTDOC files and stored the files in users C:/​Users/​AppData/​LocalLow/​Plotagon/​Plotagon directory. PLOTDOC files were JSON-formatted text files that described a Plotagon project. They listed a projects ID, name, created on date, and last updated date, before describing the project itself. When Plotagon became Plotagon Studio, PLOTDOC files were replaced by PLOT files, which are binary files that contain Plotagon Studio projects. It appears that PLOT files contain PLOTDOC files, but users can no longer access Plotagon Studios PLOTDOC files themselves. You can open a PLOTDOC file in any text editor, including Microsoft Notepad (Windows), Apple TextEdit (Mac), or GitHub Atom (cross-platform). When you do, youll be able to view the ID, name, created on date, and last updated date of the Plotagon project your PLOTDOC file represents. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Linux Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS.",
    "Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Linux Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".ANM",
    "DeluxePaint Animation",
    "4.0",
    "Contains detailed instructions for a 3D animation; typically references one or more 3D object files which are animated using the directives in the ANM file; used by several older video games as well as newer ones, such as those built for the Crytek CryENGINE. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK. Animation Viewer Mark Nine Systems Targetware Mac Mark Nine Systems Targetware Linux anim (part of GCL utilities) unanm. An ANM file is an animation created by Electronic Arts DeluxePaint Animation, a graphics and animation editing program released in 1990. It contains a series of still frames that are played in sequence to produce an animation. ANM files were used in a variety of video games, including FIFA International Soccer, Duke Nukem 3D, and Shadow Warrior. ANM file open in VLC media player Electronic Arts released a number of versions of Deluxe Paint, a bitmap graphics editing software, between 1985 and 1995. DeluxePaint Animation was Electronic Arts third Deluxe Paint release for MS-DOS PCs. Notably, it included animation creation and editing tools that allowed video game developers to create sophisticated 3D animations. These animations were saved as ANM files. An ANM file consists of a header and several up-to-64KB blocks that contain a series of still frames. Frames are stored in sequence within their blocks, but the blocks themselves may not be stored in sequence within the ANM file. For example, the last block stored within an ANM file might contain the first few frames of an animation. When a program plays an ANM file, it must first determine the order in which it should read and play back the files blocks. Because ANM files are so uncommon, most popular media players cannot play them. However, you can play ANM files in VLC media player, and you can convert ANM files to a more widely-supported video format using FFmpeg. Windows File Viewer Plus. VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpegFree.",
    "Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK. Animation Viewer Mark Nine Systems Targetware. Mac Mark Nine Systems Targetware. Linux anim (part of GCL utilities) unanm. Windows File Viewer Plus. VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".SQZ",
    "Squeeze Project File",
    "4.0",
    "An SQZ file is a project file created by Sorenson Squeeze, a program used to compress and convert videos to different file formats. It is an XML file that contains video encoding settings and a record of when and how a video was converted. SQZ files may also include settings for converting video using a cloud-based Squeeze Server. The files store only references to imported video files; they do not include actual video data. Sorenson Squeeze was a video enhancement and conversion program available for Windows and macOS. It was discontinued in 2018. Squeeze supported a wide variety of input and output video file formats, as well as many additional conversion options. Users could specify their videos container, codec, aspect ratio, and more. Users could also create videos optimized for use with YouTube, Amazon Web Services, and other online services. When a user worked with a video in Squeeze, that videos settings and version history were saved in an SQZ file. SQZ files also contain references to the locations at which videos imported into Squeeze are stored. If a user moves a video referenced in an SQZ file, the file may not load correctly in Squeeze. If you still have access to it, you can open an SQZ (Squeeze Project File) in Sorenson Squeeze (Windows, Mac). If you do not have access to Squeeze, you can open your SQZ file in any text editor, to view the XML-formatted text it contains. Windows Sorenson Squeeze Any text editor Mac Sorenson Squeeze Any text editor. An SQZ file is a backup project created by The Master Genealogist, a Windows program used to document the genealogy of people. It contains a Zip-compressed backup of a project, which includes database, documentation, and configuration files. SQZ files are meant to be opened by The Master Genealogist. But you can also manually open SQZ files with a Zip decompression program. To do this, rename the .sqz extension to .zip then extract the ZIP file to view its contents. NOTE: The Master Genealogist was discontinued in 2014. Windows Wholly Genes Software The Master Genealogist. An SQZ file is a compressed, encrypted file created by digitalSQZ Manager, a confidential file management service. It contains a file, such as a.DOCX,.XLSX,.MP4, or.PNG file, that digitalSQZ has compressed and encrypted. SQZ files can be opened only through digitalSQZ. digitalSQZ is an online service that allows users to store, compress, and encrypt sensitive files. Users can then make these files available to third parties via digitalSQZs APIs. Files that have been compressed and encrypted by digitalSQZ are saved as SQZ files. These files can be accessed only through digitalSQZ and its APIs. NOTE: digitalSQZ Manager is no longer maintained. You can open SQZ files using digitalSQZ Manager (Web). To do so, you must register for and log in to digitalSQZ Manager. Then, you will be able to access and open your SQZ files. Web digitalSQZ Manager —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows Sorenson Squeeze Any text editor. Mac Sorenson Squeeze Any text editor. Windows Wholly Genes Software The Master Genealogist. Web digitalSQZ Manager —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".SCM",
    "Super Chain Media File",
    "4.0",
    "Script written for the GIMP image editing program; used for automating actions or adding artistic effects to images opened in the GIMP editor; similar to a Photoshop plugin, but saved as a script file. GIMP scripts should be placed in the following locations for different operating systems: Mac: $HOME/​Library/​Application Support/​Gimp/​scripts/​ Windows: %UserProfile%/​.gimp-2.x/​scripts/​ Unix: $HOME/​.gimp-2.x/​scripts/​ After copying an SCM file into the scripts directory, you can refresh the list of scripts in Gimp by selecting Filters → Script-Fu → Refresh Scripts. Windows GIMP. Mac GIMP. Linux GIMPFree. Game map used by StarCraft, a real-time strategy game by Blizzard Entertainment; includes various types of terrain and resources; may be created in different sizes, including 96x96, 128x128, 192x192, and 256x256. Many maps are included with StarCraft for both solo campaigns and multi-player games. Custom maps may also be created using the Map Editor. Windows Blizzard StarCraft. Mac Blizzard StarCraft. PC screen recording created using ScreenCam screen capture software; acts as a screen camcorder that records the exact activity displayed on the screen of a Windows computer; can be streamed using StreamCam software. ScreenCam was originally developed by IBM Lotus and is now owned by SmartGuyz. Windows SmartGuyz ScreenCam. Microsoft PowerPoint with ScreenCam plug-in. Compiled script written for CLEO, a third-party scripting engine for Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas (GTA SA); enables players to expand the features of game using custom functions called opcodes; can be created using Sanny Builder, a GTA modding utility. To use an SCM file with GTA SA, it must be placed in the /​CLEO/​ directory in the game installation folder. Windows Sanny Builder. Rockstar Games Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas with CLEO installed. An SCM file is a source code file written in Scheme, a programming language developed at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT). It is typically edited with a text editor and then run using a Scheme interpreter, which reads the syntax and executes the program. SCM files can be edited with any text editor, but they are best modified using an editor that supports Scheme syntax highlighting. Scheme is part of the Lisp family of programming languages. It is most often used in academic environments for teaching functional programming concepts. Windows File Viewer Plus. Linux MIT/GNU SchemeFree. Audio or video file encoded with the SCM codec; includes digital copyright protection DRM, which guarantees the valid transmission of media over the Internet; developed by SuperMV, an audio and video interactive research company. SCM files can be played in various media players if the SuperMV SCM codec is installed. Windows Media Player Classic with SCM codec. KMPlayer with SCM codec. Microsoft Windows Media Player with SCM codec Included with OS. Archive file exported from some Samsung TVs using a USB connection; contains a list of channels saved on the television, including cable and satellite stations; used for saving exported channel lists. SCM files may be extracted and then edited with SamyGO program. However, this process is not supported by Samsung. Windows SamyGO ChanEdit. Mac SamyGO ChanEdit. Linux SamyGO ChanEditFree. Descriptor file that describes another document, such as an XML file; typically specifies the structure and formatting of the document as well as what type of data it can contain. SCM files are often found on Unix systems but may be used on other platforms as well. Other types of XML schema files include Document Type Definition (.DTD) files and W3C XML Schema (.XSD) files. Windows Any text editor Mac Any text editor Linux Any text editor.",
    "Windows GIMP. Mac GIMP. Linux GIMP. Windows Blizzard StarCraft. Mac Blizzard StarCraft. Windows SmartGuyz ScreenCam. Microsoft PowerPoint with ScreenCam plug-in. Windows Sanny Builder. Rockstar Games Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas with CLEO installed. Windows File Viewer Plus. Linux MIT/GNU Scheme. Windows Media Player Classic with SCM codec. KMPlayer with SCM codec. Microsoft Windows Media Player with SCM codec Included with OS. Windows SamyGO ChanEdit. Mac SamyGO ChanEdit. Linux SamyGO ChanEdit. Windows Any text editor. Mac Any text editor. Linux Any text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".RXR",
    "RecordXR Recording",
    "4.0",
    "An RXR file is a 3D recording saved in the RecordXR format. The virtual reality (VR) medical imaging program Medicalholodeck allows users to record sessions as RXR files. Other users can load the files in Medicalholodeck to play the recordings they contain. Medicalholodeck is a VR program that allows Windows VR and Meta Quest users to view, study, and manipulate medical images in 3D. Users who want to share a Medicalholodeck session with others (for example, a teacher who wants to share a session with their students) can save that session as an RXR file. Each RXR file contains a recording of not just a users actions during a Medicalholodeck session, but also the environment in which those actions took place. Storing a recording of the entire environment allows viewers to move around that environment while they play the recording. Viewers can also manipulate items shown in the recording. You can open an RXR file with Medicalholodeck (Windows), provided you have a compatible virtual reality headset. Windows Medicalholodeck.",
    "Windows Medicalholodeck.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".CPVC",
    "Adobe Captivate Video Composition",
    "4.0",
    "A CPVC file is a video composition created and used by Captivate, a program used to develop interactive eLearning products. It contains a video clip that can be copied, cut, or trimmed. CPVC files may also include text captions, non-interactive objects, smart shapes, images, animations, and highlight boxes. CPVC Captivate Video Compositions are similar to.CPTX Captivate Projects but is not based on the slide paradigm. After you record the video in a CPVC file, you can see it in the timeline. NOTE: You can publish CPVC files to YouTube or as an.MP4 file. Windows Adobe Captivate. Mac Adobe Captivate.",
    "Windows Adobe Captivate. Mac Adobe Captivate.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".KDENLIVE",
    "Kdenlive Project",
    "4.0",
    "A KDENLIVE file is a video editing project created by Kdenlive, a cross-platform, open-source video editor. It is saved in an XML format and contains references to the projects included audio and video files, as well as how those files are arranged on the projects editing timeline. KDENLIVE file open in Kdenlive Kdenlive is a free video editing program that allows users to import video, audio, and other media and combine those files into a single movie. Users can export their movies as.MP4,.WEBM,.MPEG2, and other types of video files. The program saves users in-progress video editing projects as KDENLIVE files. These files are text files; they do not actually include any video, audio, or media files. They contain only references to those files locations. As such, if you move a media file from the location referenced in your KDENLIVE file, your project will not load correctly in Kdenlive (as the program will not be able to find the moved media file). You can open a KDENLIVE file in Kdenlive (multiplatform). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your KDENLIVE file. If necessary, you can also open a KDENLIVE file in Microsoft Notepad (Windows), Apple TextEdit (Mac), GitHub Atom (multiplatform), or any other text editor, to view the XML data the file contains. Windows Kdenlive. Any text editor Mac Kdenlive. Any text editor Linux Kdenlive. Any text editor.",
    "Windows Kdenlive. Any text editor. Mac Kdenlive. Any text editor. Linux Kdenlive. Any text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".PIC",
    "Pictor Paint Image",
    "4.0",
    "Bitmap image created by IBM Lotus or a variety of other applications; possible programs include Advanced Art Studio, Micrografx Draw, and SoftImage 3D; should not be confused with the.PICT format. Web File Helper. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. XnViewMP. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMPFree. Deep Raster image created by Houdini, a 3D modeling and animation application; stores a run-length encoded image, including the colors, color map, and size of the picture; supports any number of planes per pixel; stores images that can be included with 3D scenes. The PIC format is proprietary and is the native format used for internal Deep Raster images saved with Houdini. Windows SideFX Houdini. Mac SideFX Houdini. Linux SideFX Houdini. A PIC file is an image file saved in the PICtor raster image format. It is the native file format used by Pictor Paint (PC Paint) and Graphics Animation System for Professionals (GRASP), which were both developed by John Bridges for the MS-DOS operating system. PICtor PIC files are uncommon since the programs that support them are no longer developed. They were often used in the 1980s and 1990s to save and share images but are now rare. If you do encounter a PIC file, it most likely is an old image created by an MS-DOS paintbrush program. The image may also be a frame of a video sequence. The PICtor format is similar to the Paintbrush Bitmap Image.PCX format. It includes a header that contains information about the display device, which allows it to be viewed on different systems. After the header, the format stores image data that may be uncompressed or compressed with Run-length encoding (RLE)compression. You can open a PIC file with PMView Pro in Windows. You can also convert the PIC file to a more common format with FFmpeg and view it with an image viewer. Windows PMView Pro. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpegFree. Image generated by Apple QuickTime or the Apple QuickDraw API; contains a raster graphic stored in the.PICT format; used for storing image captures or other still frames. Windows XnViewMP. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMPFree.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. XnViewMP. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP. Windows SideFX Houdini. Mac SideFX Houdini. Linux SideFX Houdini. Windows PMView Pro. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpeg. Windows XnViewMP. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. XnViewMP. Linux XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".MSDVD",
    "Windows DVD Maker Project File",
    "4.0",
    "DVD project created with Windows DVD Maker; formatted in XML and contains tags that define the media content, DVD title, menu style, button names, and other information; may also be generated by third-party applications that access DVD Makers encoding capabilities; does not contain actual media, only references to the locations of imported media on the computer. Windows DVD Maker is a DVD production program included with Windows Vista Home Premium and Ultimate editions. It is a supplemental application to Windows Movie Maker. NOTE: Microsoft Windows DVD Maker is no longer developed and is not supported by Windows 10. Windows Microsoft Windows DVD Maker —  (Discontinued)  Included with OS.",
    "Windows Microsoft Windows DVD Maker —  (Discontinued)  Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".WLMP",
    "Windows Live Movie Maker Project",
    "4.0",
    "A WLMP file is a movie project created by Windows Live Movie Maker, a program that allows users to create movies and slideshows. It contains paths to video, movie transitions, images, music, and effects featured in the movie project. WLMP files do not contain the actual content that appears in the movie project, only links to the content. WLMP files are typically used to create personal videos for sharing with friends and family. In Windows Live Movie Maker, you can export WLMP projects to.WMV files, publish them to YouTube, and burn them to DVDs. Windows Live Movie Maker was initially released in 2000 as part of the Windows Essentials software suite. It is primarily used to create and edit videos then share them to YouTube, Facebook, Vimeo, Flickr, or OneDrive. However, in 2012, Microsoft discontinued the Windows Live name and the program became known as just Windows Movie Maker. Microsoft then discontinued Windows Movie Maker replacing it with the Photos app that comes with Windows 10. The app includes the ability to create and edit videos with music, text, and 3D effects. The Photos app does not support the WLMP file format. You can open a WLMP file in Microsoft Windows Live Movie Maker (Windows). If you do not have access to Movie Maker, you can open your WLMP file in Nero Video (Windows). To do so, open Nero Video and then drag your WLMP file into the program. Windows Microsoft Windows Live Movie Maker —  (Discontinued)  Included with OS. Nero Video.",
    "Windows Microsoft Windows Live Movie Maker —  (Discontinued)  Included with OS. Nero Video.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".AEC",
    "Cinema 4D After Effects Composition",
    "3.9",
    "File exported by Cinema 4D, a program used for video production; saves a rendered video in a format that can be imported into Adobe After Effects, but only if the proper plug-in has been installed for After Effects; used for transferring video projects from Cinema 4D to After Effects. If your version of After Effects does not import an AEC file properly, check to make sure that you have the latest AEC importer plug-in installed. Windows Adobe After Effects 2023. Mac Adobe After Effects 2023.",
    "Windows Adobe After Effects 2023. Mac Adobe After Effects 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".BIK",
    "Bink Video File",
    "3.9",
    "Proprietary video format developed by RAD Game Tools; used for playing movie clips in video games on both PCs and console systems; allows standard video to be highly compressed while optimizing video quality for the target platform. Bink videos can be played with Windows Media Player (WMP) if you have the Windows 7 Codec Pack installed. Even though WMP says it does not recognize the .bik extension after you have installed the codec pack, choose to open the video anyway and WMP will play it. BIK files are often compressed from.AVI,.MOV, or other common video file formats. When compressed with the Bink tools, the data rates can be adjusted for resolutions as low as 320x240 up to resolutions in HD quality, thereby supporting videos that are suitable for handheld devices as well as HD TVs and computer screens. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. The RAD Video Tools. Microsoft Windows Media Player with Windows 7 Codec Pack Included with OS. Rebellion Aliens vs. Predator. VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac The Bink Video Player for MacOS X. VideoLAN VLC media player. Linux The Bink Video Player for GNU/Linux. VideoLAN VLC media playerFree. Video format used by various video games, including Sid Meiers Civilization 4 and Ghost Recon Advanced Warfighter 2; typically stored in the /Data/movies/ folder within the program folder; referenced when video clips are played within the game. Windows Take-Two Interactive Civilization 4.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. The RAD Video Tools. Microsoft Windows Media Player with Windows 7 Codec Pack Included with OS. Rebellion Aliens vs. Predator. VideoLAN VLC media player. Mac The Bink Video Player for MacOS X. VideoLAN VLC media player. Linux The Bink Video Player for GNU/Linux. VideoLAN VLC media player. Windows Take-Two Interactive Civilization 4.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".DCR",
    "Digital Court Recorder Video File",
    "3.9",
    "A DCR file is an interactive media file saved in the Shockwave format for distribution on the web. It is often used for creating web games and other highly interactive content. DCR files are similar to Flash (.SWF) files, but created with Adobe Director rather than Adobe Flash. Adobe Shockwaver Player can also open the file but runs as a web browser plug-in. NOTE: Director was originally developed by Macromedia, which was acquired by Adobe at the end of 2005. Windows Adobe Director —  (Discontinued). Trial Adobe Shockwave Player. Mac Adobe Director —  (Discontinued). Trial Adobe Shockwave PlayerFree. A DCR file is an image captured in the Kodak Digital Camera RAW (DCR) format by various Kodak digital cameras, such as the DCS 760M and DCS Pro Back Plus. It stores uncompressed or lossless image data exactly how the cameras sensor captured it. DCR files also contain metadata, such as the camera model name, sensor image dimensions, and focal length. DCR file open in Apple Preview 11 DCR is one of several proprietary camera raw formats developed by Kodak. Others include Kodak K25 (.K25), Kodak Photo-Enhancer (.KDC), and Kodak DCS200 Camera Raw (.KC2). Users that will encounter DCR files Professional and hobbyist photographers who own an older Kodak digital camera that captures images in the DCR format are most likely to encounter DCR files. For example, after shooting digital photographs in RAW mode, they may transfer their images as DCR files to their computer to view and edit them with software that supports the format. You can open DCR files with various image-editing and -viewing applications, including Microsoft Photos (with the Raw Image Extension installed), which is bundled with Windows and Apple Preview, which is bundled with macOS. Other applications that support the camera RAW format are Adobe Photoshop (Windows and macOS), Adobe Photoshop Elements (Windows and macOS), ACD Systems ACDSee (Windows), and Adobe Photoshop Express (Android and iOS). Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Microsoft Photos Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop Elements. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Kodak DCS File Converter. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. iOS Adobe Photoshop Express. Android File Viewer for Android. Adobe Photoshop ExpressFree. A DCR file is a component resource file created and used by Delphi, a Windows, OS X, Android, and iOS IDE. It contains a compiled resource, which includes a bitmap image that is used as a component icon for the component palette. DCR files should not be deleted. The DCR file is the same as the binary.RES file generated by Delph. However, it is used to store the component icon instead of the applications main icon. NOTE: The Delphi IDE includes an image editor that can open and create DCR files. Windows Embarcadero Delphi. Video file created by High Criterias Liberty video recording software products, such as Liberty Court Recorder, Liberty Police Interview Recorder, and Liberty Meeting Recorder; used for storing audio and video recorded in courtrooms, police interviews, and city council meetings. DCR files can be played back using the free Liberty Court Player, which is available for Mac, Windows, iOS, and Android platforms. NOTE: The DCR format used by Liberty software differs from the DCR format used by BIS Digital Digital Court Recorder, even though the two products are often used for the same purpose. Windows High Criteria Liberty Court Recorder. High Criteria Liberty Player. Mac High Criteria Liberty Player. iOS High Criteria Liberty Player. Android High Criteria Liberty PlayerFree. Video file created by Digital Court Recorder (DCR), a program used for recording live video of courtroom proceedings; may include typed notes in addition to the recorded video; can be played back using BIS Digitals free DCR Player. Windows BIS Digital DCR Player. BIS Digital Digital Court Recorder. Mac BIS Digital DCR Player. BIS Digital Digital Court Recorder.",
    "Windows Adobe Director —  (Discontinued). Trial Adobe Shockwave Player. Mac Adobe Director —  (Discontinued). Trial Adobe Shockwave Player. Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Microsoft Photos Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop Elements. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Kodak DCS File Converter. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe Photoshop Elements. iOS Adobe Photoshop Express. Android File Viewer for Android. Adobe Photoshop Express. Windows Embarcadero Delphi. Windows High Criteria Liberty Court Recorder. High Criteria Liberty Player. Mac High Criteria Liberty Player. iOS High Criteria Liberty Player. Android High Criteria Liberty Player. Windows BIS Digital DCR Player. BIS Digital Digital Court Recorder. Mac BIS Digital DCR Player. BIS Digital Digital Court Recorder.",
    "Various applications, including Adobe Photoshop and ACD Systems ACDSee, can convert DCR files to other formats. For example, Photoshop can convert DCR files to many file types, including the following formats:.DNG - Digital Negative Image.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIF - Tagged Image File Format.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.WEBP - WebP Image.BMP - Bitmap Image.PSD - Adobe Photoshop Document."],
    ["video_files",
    ".MSWMM",
    "Windows Movie Maker Project",
    "3.9",
    "An MSWMM file is a movie created with Windows Movie Maker. It contains a project, which includes the movie timeline, transitions, and references to video clips, audio files, and still images used by the movie. Windows Movie Maker allows the user to combine and edit content saved within an MSWMM file. Once the movie is finished, it can be exported in a standard video format or burned to a DVD. You can convert an MSWMM file to a.WMV file, which is a more common format, using Window MovieMaker: Windows Vista - Open the MSWMM file by selecting File → Open Project. Then select [m[File → Publish Movie[/m] and follow the prompts to save the file as a WMV file. Windows 7 - Open the MSWMM file by selecting File → Open Project. Then, drag the project to the timeline and click Save to my computer, which is under Finish Movie in the left pane. Then follow the prompts in the wizard to save the file as a WMV file. You can also convert MSWMM files using Wondershare Video Converter. With this program, you can convert the project to more popular formats, such as.MP4,.AVI,.FLV,.MOV,.DVD,.VOB, an.MPG. Windows Microsoft Windows Live Movie Maker —  (Discontinued)  Included with OS. Microsoft Windows Movie Maker —  (Discontinued)  Included with OS. Wondershare Video Converter Pro. Mac Wondershare Video Converter Pro for Mac.",
    "Windows Microsoft Windows Live Movie Maker —  (Discontinued)  Included with OS. Microsoft Windows Movie Maker —  (Discontinued)  Included with OS. Wondershare Video Converter Pro. Mac Wondershare Video Converter Pro for Mac.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".AMC",
    "AMC Video File",
    "3.9",
    "An AMC file is a video file created in the Adaptive Modulation and Coding (AMC) format. It is designed for transmitting multimedia data between mobile devices. You will most likely only encounter AMC files if you use a mobile device that utilizes cellular services provided by the KDDI Corporation, which is a Japanese telecommunication operator. The AMC format is a variation of the more common 3GPP format (.3GP files) that allows video quality to be negotiated based on the channel conditions between cellular devices. If you do acquire an AMC video file, you can play it with Apple QuickTime Player and PEGASYS TMPGEnc MovieStyle. However, due to limitations with the AMC format, recorded audio may not be played with the video. Windows PEGASYS TMPGEnc MovieStyle. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Data file created by Ant Movie Catalog, a program used for organizing collections of movies, DVDs, CDs, and tapes; stores information for different movie titles, such as the title, director, producer, year, and video format; can be displayed in HTML format for reviewing and sharing with others. Windows Ant Movie CatalogFree.",
    "Windows PEGASYS TMPGEnc MovieStyle. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Windows Ant Movie Catalog.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".WEBM",
    "WebM Video",
    "3.9",
    "A WEBM file is a video saved in the WebM format, an open, royalty-free format designed for sharing video on the web. WebM uses a container structure similar to the Matroska (.MKV) video format, which stores both audio and video data. Video is compressed using a VP8 or VP9 codec, and audio is compressed with either the Vorbis or Opus audio codec. WEBM file open in VideoLAN VLC media player 3 Several modern web browsers, such as Chrome, Edge, and Firefox, include built-in support for the WebM format. If your browser does not support WebM (e.g. Safari or Internet Explorer), you will need to install a WebM plug-in to play WebM media files. WebM is an open-source, royalty-free alternative to the patented H.264 and H.265 standards. Since it is 100% free, the technology is suitable for commercial and non-commercial applications. NOTE: Google acquired ON2, the original developer of VP8 technology, in 2010. The WebM Project represents Google in the Alliance for Open Media. Since the WebM format was designed for the web, WEBM files are typically embedded in webpages (using an HTML5 <video> tag). In most cases, you can play a WebM audio or video file within a web browser using the on-screen controls. If you get an error saying your browser does not support the WebM format, you can download the free WebM plug-in, install it in your browser, and then reload the page. If you encounter a WEBM file offline, you can play it in VideoLAN VLC media player (multiplatform), File Viewer Plus (Windows), or Eltima Elmedia Player (Mac). Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. VideoLAN VLC media player. Miro Video Converter. HandBrake. Microsoft Windows Media Player with DirectShow Filter Included with OS. Microsoft Edge. Microsoft Internet Explorer with VP8 plug-in. Mozilla Firefox. Google Chrome. Opera. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Miro Video Converter. HandBrake. ShedWorx Smart Converter. Mozilla Firefox. Google Chrome. Opera. Eltima Elmedia Player. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. HandBrake. Mozilla Firefox. Opera. iOS VideoLAN VLC for Mobile. olimsoft OPlayer. PentaLoop PlayerXtreme Media Player. Android File Viewer for Android. Videolabs VLC for AndroidFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. VideoLAN VLC media player. Miro Video Converter. HandBrake. Microsoft Windows Media Player with DirectShow Filter Included with OS. Microsoft Edge. Microsoft Internet Explorer with VP8 plug-in. Mozilla Firefox. Google Chrome. Opera. Mac VideoLAN VLC media player. Miro Video Converter. HandBrake. ShedWorx Smart Converter. Mozilla Firefox. Google Chrome. Opera. Eltima Elmedia Player. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. FFmpeg. HandBrake. Mozilla Firefox. Opera. iOS VideoLAN VLC for Mobile. olimsoft OPlayer. PentaLoop PlayerXtreme Media Player. Android File Viewer for Android. Videolabs VLC for Android.",
    "VideoLAN VLC media player (multiplatform), HandBrake (multiplatform), and Miro Video Converter (Windows, Mac) can all convert WEBM files to other video formats. For example, VLC can convert WEBM videos to:.MP4 - MPEG-4 Video.TS - Video Transport Stream.ASF - Advanced Systems Format."],
    ["video_files",
    ".SCM",
    "ScreenCam Screen Recording",
    "3.9",
    "Script written for the GIMP image editing program; used for automating actions or adding artistic effects to images opened in the GIMP editor; similar to a Photoshop plugin, but saved as a script file. GIMP scripts should be placed in the following locations for different operating systems: Mac: $HOME/​Library/​Application Support/​Gimp/​scripts/​ Windows: %UserProfile%/​.gimp-2.x/​scripts/​ Unix: $HOME/​.gimp-2.x/​scripts/​ After copying an SCM file into the scripts directory, you can refresh the list of scripts in Gimp by selecting Filters → Script-Fu → Refresh Scripts. Windows GIMP. Mac GIMP. Linux GIMPFree. Game map used by StarCraft, a real-time strategy game by Blizzard Entertainment; includes various types of terrain and resources; may be created in different sizes, including 96x96, 128x128, 192x192, and 256x256. Many maps are included with StarCraft for both solo campaigns and multi-player games. Custom maps may also be created using the Map Editor. Windows Blizzard StarCraft. Mac Blizzard StarCraft. PC screen recording created using ScreenCam screen capture software; acts as a screen camcorder that records the exact activity displayed on the screen of a Windows computer; can be streamed using StreamCam software. ScreenCam was originally developed by IBM Lotus and is now owned by SmartGuyz. Windows SmartGuyz ScreenCam. Microsoft PowerPoint with ScreenCam plug-in. Compiled script written for CLEO, a third-party scripting engine for Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas (GTA SA); enables players to expand the features of game using custom functions called opcodes; can be created using Sanny Builder, a GTA modding utility. To use an SCM file with GTA SA, it must be placed in the /​CLEO/​ directory in the game installation folder. Windows Sanny Builder. Rockstar Games Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas with CLEO installed. An SCM file is a source code file written in Scheme, a programming language developed at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT). It is typically edited with a text editor and then run using a Scheme interpreter, which reads the syntax and executes the program. SCM files can be edited with any text editor, but they are best modified using an editor that supports Scheme syntax highlighting. Scheme is part of the Lisp family of programming languages. It is most often used in academic environments for teaching functional programming concepts. Windows File Viewer Plus. Linux MIT/GNU SchemeFree. Audio or video file encoded with the SCM codec; includes digital copyright protection DRM, which guarantees the valid transmission of media over the Internet; developed by SuperMV, an audio and video interactive research company. SCM files can be played in various media players if the SuperMV SCM codec is installed. Windows Media Player Classic with SCM codec. KMPlayer with SCM codec. Microsoft Windows Media Player with SCM codec Included with OS. Archive file exported from some Samsung TVs using a USB connection; contains a list of channels saved on the television, including cable and satellite stations; used for saving exported channel lists. SCM files may be extracted and then edited with SamyGO program. However, this process is not supported by Samsung. Windows SamyGO ChanEdit. Mac SamyGO ChanEdit. Linux SamyGO ChanEditFree. Descriptor file that describes another document, such as an XML file; typically specifies the structure and formatting of the document as well as what type of data it can contain. SCM files are often found on Unix systems but may be used on other platforms as well. Other types of XML schema files include Document Type Definition (.DTD) files and W3C XML Schema (.XSD) files. Windows Any text editor Mac Any text editor Linux Any text editor.",
    "Windows GIMP. Mac GIMP. Linux GIMP. Windows Blizzard StarCraft. Mac Blizzard StarCraft. Windows SmartGuyz ScreenCam. Microsoft PowerPoint with ScreenCam plug-in. Windows Sanny Builder. Rockstar Games Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas with CLEO installed. Windows File Viewer Plus. Linux MIT/GNU Scheme. Windows Media Player Classic with SCM codec. KMPlayer with SCM codec. Microsoft Windows Media Player with SCM codec Included with OS. Windows SamyGO ChanEdit. Mac SamyGO ChanEdit. Linux SamyGO ChanEdit. Windows Any text editor. Mac Any text editor. Linux Any text editor.",
    "?"],
