    "3.9",
    "Video recording created by SeeVogh Player, an application that allows you to record, playback, and edit SeeVogh meetings; contains a standard video recording of a meeting. NOTE: If your original EVO file becomes corrupted, you can use the Repair SeeVogh/EVO recordings tool to recreate a new EVO file. Windows SeeVogh Player Mac SeeVogh Player Linux SeeVogh Player. High definition video file from an HD DVD disc; stores the movies main audio/video data; similar to a.VOB file on a standard DVD; can be played by various PC video playback programs. NOTE: The HD DVD format is not commonly used, as Blu-ray has become the standard format used for high definition video. Windows CyberLink PowerDVD 21. JRiver Media Center. Microsoft Windows Media Player with Windows 7 Codec Pack Included with OS. EVODemux.",
