    "Surveillance Video File",
    "3.6",
    "Video format used by multiple video surveillance systems; typically contains video recordings captured on closed-circuit television (CCTV) devices; may be saved as a backup file, which can usually be viewed with the software included with the video camera system. Windows HiSystem DVR System Plus INTOTECH SmartDVR Formula Silicon DSS Backup Manager. Virus that uses the reverse extension of an.AVI file; scans for files stored in a REQUEST.IVA file and copies the files found into an archive called RECEIPT.IVA.. NOTE: Files with an .iva extension should be scanned with antivirus software or deleted immediately. Windows Should not be opened.",
