    ["video_files",
    ".OGM",
    "Ogg Media File",
    "3.3",
    "An OGM file contains a matrix book created by Origin, a scientific and engineering data analysis and graphing application. It stores one or more matrix sheets, which include columns and rows of numbers, special characters, or spaces. OGM files also store other information about the matrix, such as the names of the sheets, math functions, matrix dimensions, style and formatting, and data type. You can open OGM files with Origin and Origin Viewer. Origin is only available for Windows and is the primary program used to create, open, and edit OGM files. When open in Origin, the matrix appears as a window in an open project (.OPJ or.OPJU file). Origin Viewer is also commonly used to view OGM files since it is free and can be used in Windows and macOS. To open an OGM file in Origin, select File → Open.., select the Origin Window.ogm file type, navigate to the OGM file location, and click Open. You can save Origin matrices as templates in order to preserve settings to be used with other matrices you create. To do this, select File → Save Template As.. and Origin will create an.OTM file to store the template. NOTE: The release of Origin 2018 included an updated unicode format for saving matrices (.OGMU), which features performance advantages over the older, non-unicode OGM file format. Windows OriginLab Origin. OriginLab Origin Viewer. Mac OriginLab Origin ViewerFree. Compressed video file that uses an altered form of Xiph.Orgs Ogg file container format; supports playback of video content that incorporates DirectShow filters; created as an extension to the Ogg specification so that Windows Media Player (older versions) and other programs could easily play Ogg video and audio files. NOTE: Xiph.Org, the owner and developer of the Ogg specification, does not support the OGM format because it lies outside of the Ogg specification. The OGM format is different than the format used for.OGG and.OGV files. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. MPUI. MPlayer. VideoLAN VLC media player. NCH Prism. mpv. Mac MPlayer. VideoLAN VLC media player. mpv. Linux Totem. MPlayer. VideoLAN VLC media player. mpvFree.",
    "Windows OriginLab Origin. OriginLab Origin Viewer. Mac OriginLab Origin Viewer. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. MPUI. MPlayer. VideoLAN VLC media player. NCH Prism. mpv. Mac MPlayer. VideoLAN VLC media player. mpv. Linux Totem. MPlayer. VideoLAN VLC media player. mpv.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".MOI",
    "MOI Video File",
    "3.3",
    "File created by digital camcorders to store information about a.MOD MPEG-2 video recording; contains data such as version, date, duration, codec, and bitrate; used by a range of video recorders, including the JVC Everio series, the Canon FS100, and some Panasonic camcorders. NOTE: MOI files do not contain actual video data. They are only used for describing a corresponding MOD file. To convert a MOD file to another video format, use a MOD converter program such as iOrgSoft Mod Converter. Windows iOrgsoft MOD Converter. Mac iOrgsoft MOD Converter for Mac.",
    "Windows iOrgsoft MOD Converter. Mac iOrgsoft MOD Converter for Mac.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".MP5",
    "Chinese Portable Media Player Video",
    "3.3",
    "An MP5 file is a video that is meant to be played on a Chinese MP5 portable media player. MP5 files are not significantly different from.MP4 files. Like MP4 files, MP5 files are encoded using the MPEG-4 or MPEG-H codecs. The only difference between MP5 files and MP4 files is that MP5 files are often encoded such that are optimized for MP5 media players. In an attempt to set themselves apart from other media players, many Chinese portable media players advertise themselves as MP5 players. However, there is no real MP5 file format. The MP5 files these media players use are simply renamed MP4 files. Most MP5 files are encoded using the H.264/AVC, or MPEG-4, codec. Thus, if you change the files extension to.mp4, you can often play them in any MP4 media player. You can play MP5 videos as-is in some Chinese media players, such as Baidu Player and QvodPlayer. However, the easiest way to play an MP5 file is likely to change its extension to.mp4 and play it an MP4 media player, such as VideoLAN VLC media player (cross-platform). Android Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player Windows Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player Mac Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player Linux Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player iOS Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player Chrome OS Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player.",
    "Android Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player. Windows Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player. Mac Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player. Linux Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player. iOS Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player. Chrome OS Change extension to MP4 and play in MP4 media player.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".NUT",
    "NUT Video File",
    "3.3",
    "Video file saved in the NUT Open Container Format, a container format similar to.AVI,.ASF, and.MKV; supports several different audio and video codecs as well as subtitle information. The NUT format was developed by the MPlayer, FFmpeg, and Libav teams. However, it did not gained wide popularity and therefore is an uncommon video format. Windows File Viewer Plus. MPlayer. FFmpeg. Mac MPlayer. FFmpeg. Eltima Elmedia Player. Linux MPlayer. FFmpeg. iOS iFunia VideoConvert for iPad. A NUT file is a text file that contains Squirrel code written in the Squirrel programming language. It is a script used as a plugin to extend functionality of a program and for scripted events in video games. Squirrel is an object-oriented programming language similar to Lua, C++, and JavaScript. it is designed to be lightweight, fitting the memory, size, and real-time requirements of programs, mainly video games, such as Left 4 Dead 2, Simutrans, Shadow Warrior, SuperTux, and Portal 2. Since there is another file type with the .nut extension, you can look at the file size for an indication of what type of NUT file you have. NUT files containing a Squirrel script rarely reach 1MB whereas NUT video files are larger than 1MB. Windows Squirrel. Mac Squirrel. Linux SquirrelFree. A NUT file is a texture file used by a Bandai Namco video game. It contains a skin that is applied to an in-game character, object, or level. NUT files are most notably used in Super Smash Bros. for WiiU and Nintendo 3DS. Most 3D video game characters are comprised of a 3D model, texture, and animation files. The texture file serves as the characters skin, providing the look of their skin, clothing, and other items. When you play a game, the game applies the characters texture file to their 3D model (usually saved as a wireframe skeleton), creating the characters in-game appearance. The same process is used to skin in-game items and levels. Some Bandai Namco video games use texture files that are saved in the NUT file format. Because Super Smash Bros. 4 is the most popular game that uses NUT files, Super Smash Bros. 4 modders are most likely to encounter the files. However, other Bandai Namco games, such as Taiko no Tatsujin Tokumori, also use NUT files. NOTE: The 3D models used with NUT files are saved in the.NUD format. You can open NUT (Namco Universal Texture) files in Smash Forge, an open-source Super Smash Bros. 4 file editor and modding tool. To do so, select File → Open → Open File from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your NUT file. Windows Smash ForgeFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus. MPlayer. FFmpeg. Mac MPlayer. FFmpeg. Eltima Elmedia Player. Linux MPlayer. FFmpeg. iOS iFunia VideoConvert for iPad. Windows Squirrel. Mac Squirrel. Linux Squirrel. Windows Smash Forge.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".M2P",
    "MPEG-2 Program Stream File",
    "3.3",
    "Video container format that supports MPEG-2 audio and video compression; similar to an MPEG-1 file, but also supports interlaced video and more audio channels; commonly used for streaming digital video. NOTE: M2P files are generally used for streaming media. Standard MPEG-2 video files typically have an.MPG extension, while standard MPEG-2 audio files usually have an.MP2 extension. Windows Roxio Creator NXT Pro 9. Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. Media Player Classic. VideoLAN VLC media player. Elecard MPEG Player. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Roxio Toast 20. Squared 5 MPEG Streamclip. iOS PentaLoop PlayerXtreme Media Player. Plugin installation pack for the Maxthon Web browser; includes a compressed add-on for Maxthon that provides additional features and capabilities within the program. M2P files are essentially.ZIP files renamed with a .m2p extension. They can be installed by double-clicking the file or dragging the file into an open Maxthon browser window. Windows MaxthonFree.",
    "Windows Roxio Creator NXT Pro 9. Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. Media Player Classic. VideoLAN VLC media player. Elecard MPEG Player. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Roxio Toast 20. Squared 5 MPEG Streamclip. iOS PentaLoop PlayerXtreme Media Player. Windows Maxthon.",
    "?"],
    ["video_files",
    ".VP3",
    "On2 Streaming Video File",
    "3.3",
    "Streaming video file compressed on-demand using the VP3 video codec; contains compressed video at variable compression rates; used to send the highest video quality possible given bandwidth adjustments and fluctuations. VP3 files can be played in Windows Media Player and QuickTime provided they have the appropriate codec installed. The VP3 format was created by On2 Technologies, and is now maintained by Xiph.org Foundation, who has updated the VP3 format to the Theora format. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. A VP3 file is a computer-aided manufacturing (CAM) file saved in version 3 of the Husqvarna Viking / Pfaff format (VP3). It stores embroidery stitch information for a Pfaff or Husqvarna Viking sewing machine to stitch a pattern onto a piece of fabric. VP3 files contain information about one or more designs (typically just one) organized into StitchBlocks, which are sets of continuous stitches in a specific color. VP3 file open in BERNINA ARTlink 8 Pfaff and Husqvarna developed the VP3 format to replace the.VIP and.PCS embroidery pattern files used by older Pfaff and Husqvarna sewing machines. Older Pfaff models, such as the 7570, 7562, 7550, and 1400 series, utilize PCS files. Newer models, such as 2124, 2134, 2170, 2144, and 2140 use VP3 files. What is the data structure of a VP3 file? The VP3 format improves upon older formats by supporting extra design information, which has become necessary as patterns have grown more advanced and complex. The VP3 format typically consists of the following structure: File Header and Data - Includes metadata, hoop and design information, and the number of stitch blocks in the file. Design Block - Includes ColorBlocks, which are organized into StitchBlocks that store stitch information. Additional Design Blocks - Includes ColorBlocks for an additional design block. Most VP3 files only have one design block. How do I transfer a VP3 file from my computer to a sewing machine? To transfer a VP3 file to a sewing machine, insert a USB storage device in your computer. Then, transfer the VP3 file from your computer to the connected storage device via File Explorer in Windows or Finder in macOS. After transferring the file, eject the storage device from your computer and insert it into the Pfaff or Husqvarna Viking sewing machine to transfer the design to embroider it onto the material. If your sewing machine is Wifi-enabled, you can download the design directly to the machine via the machines touchscreen interface. NOTE: Husqvarna Viking and Pfaff sewing machines are owned by SGSB Co. Ltd. You can open VP3 files with various applications, including BERNINA ARTlink (Windows), Wings Systems my editor (Windows), PREMIER+ Embroidery (multiplatform), and Wilcom TrueSizer (Windows). These apps enable you to convert VP3 files to other embroidery and image formats, such as.PES,.JEF,.JPG, and.PNG. You can also view and convert VP3 files to other formats with the Embroidery Viewer and Converter web application and plugin for the Google Chrome web browser. If you are an Android user, you can use Touch Embroidery. and Embroidery Viewer to open VP3 files. Windows BERNINA ARTlink. Wings Systems my editor. Wilcom TrueSizer —  (Discontinued). Trial PREMIER+ Embroidery. Google Chrome with Embroidery Viewer and Converter plugin. Mac PREMIER+ Embroidery. Google Chrome with Embroidery Viewer and Converter plugin. Linux Google Chrome with Embroidery Viewer and Converter plugin. Web Embroidery Viewer and Converter. Android Embroidermodder Team Embroidery Viewer. David Olsen Touch Embroidery. Chrome OS Embroidery Viewer and ConverterFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Windows BERNINA ARTlink. Wings Systems my editor. Wilcom TrueSizer —  (Discontinued). Trial PREMIER+ Embroidery. Google Chrome with Embroidery Viewer and Converter plugin. Mac PREMIER+ Embroidery. Google Chrome with Embroidery Viewer and Converter plugin. Linux Google Chrome with Embroidery Viewer and Converter plugin. Web Embroidery Viewer and Converter. Android Embroidermodder Team Embroidery Viewer. David Olsen Touch Embroidery. Chrome OS Embroidery Viewer and Converter.",
    "?"],
