    "3.3",
    "Ripped DVD package created by RipIt, a program used to make digital backups of DVDs; contains audio and video files ripped from a DVD; used for backing up DVDs and playing them with Apple DVD Player. RipIt cannot burn new DVDs with DVDMEDIA files. However, it can export ripped DVDs to the standard DVD format (VIDEO_TS and AUDIO_TS directories) for burning with other DVD burning utilities. To export ripped DVDs to the standard DVD format, either 1) uncheck the preferences option use.dvdmedia extension in RipIt before ripping a DVD, or 2) right click the DVDMEDIA file and select Show Package Contents. Windows HandBrake. Mac The Little App Factory RipIt. Apple DVD Player Included with OS. iSkysoft DVD Ripper 4. VideoLAN VLC media player. HandBrake. Linux HandBrakeFree.",
