    ["video_files",
    ".WRF",
    "WebEx Recording",
    "3.2",
    "A WRF file is a video recording created by Cisco WebEx Recorder, a screen-recording program that is an extension of Cisco WebEx. Typically, WRF files contain training videos or demonstrations. The files can be played in Cisco WebEx Player, which is freely available on WebExs website. WebEx users can use the WebEx Recorder to record the actions they perform on their PC and an audio walkthrough of those actions, creating a training video or demonstration to be shared with other WebEx users. These recordings are saved as WRF files. WRF files use a proprietary video format that is recognized only by WebEx Recorder, Player, and Recording Editor. To watch the video a WRF file contains outside WebExs players, you must convert the file to a more common video file format, such as.WMV. How do I convert WRF files to WMV files? You can use the Cisco WebEx WRF2WMV Converter to convert a WRF file to a WMV file. WMV files can be played in many media players, including Microsoft Windows Media Player and VideoLAN VLC media player. You can open and play a WRF file in Cisco WebEx Player (Windows, Mac). To do so, download, install, and open WebEx Player, and then select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your WRF file. Mac Cisco WebEx Player. Windows Cisco WebEx Player. Cisco WebEx WRF2WMVFree.",
    "Mac Cisco WebEx Player. Windows Cisco WebEx Player. Cisco WebEx WRF2WMV.",
    "?"],
