    ".WMD",
    "Windows Media Download Package",
    "3.2",
    "Zip compressed file used by Windows Media Player; may store multimedia content, playlists, and borders (custom interfaces); used as a format for downloading audio and video over the Internet. WMD files are.ZIP files that use the .wmd extension so that Windows Media Player opens them by default. You can decompress them manually with any Zip-compatible decompression utility. Windows Microsoft Windows Media Player Included with OS.",
