    ".MOOV",
    "Apple QuickTime Movie",
    "3.2",
    "Movie file used for saving compressed movies in a common multimedia format; contains compressed audio and video data; format developed by Apple, but now recognized as cross-platform. MOOV files are more commonly seen with a.MOV extension. .moov was originally used as the default Macintosh extension, and .mov was used for Windows QuickTime (which is now discontinued). However, .mov later became the accepted extension for both platforms. Windows Roxio Creator NXT Pro 9. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Roxio Toast 20. Roxio Popcorn. iOS PentaLoop PlayerXtreme Media Player.",
